# Terminates HTTPS on the standard port and reverse-proxies to the Flask
# app, which listens on an internal-only port (127.0.0.1:5000, not exposed
# outside the VM).
#
# Uses a manually-generated certificate (see generate-cert.sh), not Caddy's
# own `tls internal` — that directive tries to install its generated root CA
# into the VM's system trust store, which the unprivileged caddy service
# account can't do, and per Caddy's own docs that failure has no supported
# workaround. In testing it left the certificate-issuing pipeline broken
# (every TLS handshake failed with a generic internal-error alert), so this
# sidesteps that subsystem entirely. Every device still needs the same
# one-time "trust this certificate" step on first visit — see DEPLOY.md's
# last section for upgrading to a real, browser-trusted Let's Encrypt
# certificate once you have a domain (even a free one), which doesn't have
# this problem since it doesn't touch the local trust store at all.
{
	admin off
}

:443 {
	tls /etc/caddy/tls/cert.pem /etc/caddy/tls/key.pem
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}
